%N A399419 Number of nonisomorphic simple hypergraphs with n vertices and trivial automorphism group, allowing isolated vertices and excluding the empty edge.
%C A399419 A simple hypergraph with trivial automorphism group can have at most one isolated vertex (this gives 2nd formula).
%F A399419 a(n) = Sum_{[H] <= S_n} mu(1,H)*2^o(H)/|N_{S_n}(H)|, where the sum is over conjugacy classes of subgroups H of S_n, mu is the subgroup-lattice Moebius function, N_{S_n}(H) is the normalizer of H in S_n, and o(H) is the number of H-orbits on the nonempty subsets of [n].
%F A399419 a(n) = A330295(n) + A330295(n-1) = A330294(n) - A330294(n-2) for n >= 2.
%e A399419 For n=3 there are 8 nonisomorphic simple hypergraphs with trivial automorphism group, so a(3)=8.
%Y A399419 Cf. A330294, A330295, A330229, A330282, A330343.
